#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096447 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48a66a99-6b4a-5ad5-8922-6f48006ff183" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "2a61b115-4e26-5966-b2a9-d2fedef6b728" :question/math-academy-id "e-4282" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ has magnitude $3$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$." :question/worked-solution "To obtain the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$, we divide $\\mathbf{a}$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=\\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096448 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44ac67b-5e3d-5b1e-bf2c-554b592ba29e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Vector Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "23d9a601-974b-51c2-a6ea-0ebadde19efc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4283" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $10$, while the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $20$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a+b}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $\\mathbf{a+b}$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}$ goes from the tail of $\\mathbf{a}$ to the head of $\\mathbf{b}$:\n\n![](images/32/32c48d8c19fc68fbc172b240ded922f3e2ebc12804411c318ff63fe999aaedcc.png)\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $\\mathbf{a+b}$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, first notice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}a + b & ^{2} &= & a & ^{2} +\\left.\\end{vmatrix}b\\right|^{2} \\\\\n&= 10^{2} + 20^{2} \\\\\n&= 100 + 400 \\\\\n&= 500\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\mathbf{a+b} &= \\sqrt{500}=10\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + b}{\\mid a + b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10\\sqrt{5}}(a + b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096493 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "6dfe09f0-30e2-53bc-a8f6-d7e4a3b8232a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5181" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3042242136b82b867b8bd7911761ee38318924df0c9979488d20f04117c45d9.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf a$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/b3/b316448c885a20a7ed60871ce0f1a4dc4f77bd4658dc6eda3407fb3c89a088cb.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\angle AHB = 90^\\circ\n$$\n\n, $AH=3$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^{2} + BH^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{9 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$ is $\\sqrt{13}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{\\mid a \\mid} \\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b11642dd-80cc-539c-8c2d-8cdee58e9d3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector in a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae96c78f-e10d-563b-82af-e2c02160928e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094940} {:answer/id #uuid "25f7a90e-939a-568d-ba3d-07a616fcb021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094941} {:answer/id #uuid "328e6ad2-ef2f-5827-8881-60cdfaebb76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2q}{\\sqrt{13}} + \\frac{r}{\\sqrt{29}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094942} {:answer/id #uuid "681555fa-cdb3-5281-b943-0cf1eed80c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(q + r))/(\\sqrt{73})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094943} {:answer/id #uuid "703e463a-8826-5adf-9d3d-36bfd8037d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{q + r}{\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094944}] :answer-field/id #uuid "96962338-e491-50f7-b8da-1efc8b69ba83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094939}] :question/id #uuid "9d05ca0e-131b-5294-8367-1760396e4369" :question/math-academy-id "q-19276" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9dfaf74a497a2fd22428e09a4c26d573e184c9728ccf67f11ebb9d6a2a44f4c6.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $q + r$?"}]}
